{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1023542-sell-me-btp-in-one-sentence","id":1023542,"title":"Sell me BtP in one sentence","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-28T19:03:56-08:00","id":1023542,"title":"Sell me BtP in one sentence","content":"So... I backed z Beast during a Kichstarter campaign, got my pdf and still waiting for the book copy. But to be honest I don't know much about the game and why is it cool. So far Wee Wolf, Changeling, nad recently Mage are my top CoD games. What's cool about Beast? Why Is the game worth playing? And most importantly can it be conveniently played in solo game? Currently I'm living in China, with my wife as the only player for now, so I don't have much choice in this matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2637-qendi","name":"qendi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T20:55:52-08:00","id":1023568,"title":"","content":"So many of what the developers and the fans of a game market as its selling point often turn out to be the turn-off point for others. It's hard to point out one feature of the game without knowing your tastes.<br /> <br /> Anyways, Beast is a game about playing people who have a nightmare-monster spawned from the collective legends of humanity as their soul. Remember how the WoD and CofD games are about playing the monsters instead of the humans? Well, Beast takes that to its logical end and allows you to play the truly legendary monsters - the Jotunn, the Nemean Lion, the Griffin, the Kraken, the Roc, and the ever-popular Dragon - such things. It also gives you room for more modern horrors like the Slenderman, or completely made-up ones of your choosing. Chinese legends and myths are rich with such monsters, so you have a wide range of choices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T22:58:23-08:00","id":1023598,"title":"","content":"You can play Dracula from Wallachia and Dracula from Castlevania as the same character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T00:32:17-08:00","id":1023613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>qendi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1023542-sell-me-btp-in-one-sentence#post1023542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... I backed z Beast during a Kichstarter campaign, got my pdf and still waiting for the book copy. But to be honest I don't know much about the game and why is it cool. So far Wee Wolf, Changeling, nad recently Mage are my top CoD games. What's cool about Beast? Why Is the game worth playing? And most importantly can it be conveniently played in solo game? Currently I'm living in China, with my wife as the only player for now, so I don't have much choice in this matter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> While the other games in the series are largely focused on their own specific setting, Beast the Primordial is built for and encourages cross over games between multiple splats. Now you can have Changelings, Vampires, Werewolves, Mages, Mummies and more all working together under one roof, instead of trying to maim and kill each other. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T04:08:56-08:00","id":1023665,"title":"","content":"Pro-cross-over would be an asset... If I wasn't playing solo games;/ <br /> <br /> @21C Hermit: So sell me what do you think is the most awesome about the game. So far I disliked only one CoD game and it was Promethean 1ed (I don't know 2ed though).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2637-qendi","name":"qendi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T04:27:18-08:00","id":1023670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>qendi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1023542-sell-me-btp-in-one-sentence?p=1023665#post1023665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pro-cross-over would be an asset... If I wasn't playing solo games;/<br /> <br /> @21C Hermit: So sell me what do you think is the most awesome about the game. So far I disliked only one CoD game and it was Promethean 1ed (I don't know 2ed though).</div> </div> </div> </div>Playing a legendary monster straight from the stories. Positioning youself as the Big Bad who is supposed to get his ass kicked by the Designated Good Guy Protagonist, then subverting the plot to seize the role of the Main Character for yourself.<br /> <br /> I've had that moment where I knew - not <i>felt</i>, <b>knew </b>- that I'm nowhere as important to the world as I want to be, nor as awesome as I want to be, but someone <i>else </i>out there is.<br /> I've also had that moment where I had some pretty deep-seated and wrecked shit somewhere inside me, thankfully kept in check by a well-developed superego, well-internalized ethics, and no particular genetic/psychological quirks that would hinder me from taming it, but still biding its time there regardless.<br /> <br /> Beast &quot;can be&quot; (not necessarily &quot;is&quot;) about people who qualify for one or both of those qualities that are suddenly empowered to let go and run wild.<br /> <hr /><br /> Side tracking here, but Promethean 2E is about exploring humanity from outside - all its ups and downs. It is also about alchemically Created proto-men who badly need to stabilize themselves before they inflict entropy on everything. And it turns out becoming human, which are apparently the base material out of which the world is made out of, is enough to do just that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T15:55:10-08:00","id":1023977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>qendi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1023542-sell-me-btp-in-one-sentence?p=1023665#post1023665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pro-cross-over would be an asset... If I wasn't playing solo games;/<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Doesn't mean you can't have the cross NPC characters. :P<br /> <br /> And speaking of cross overs, I forgot to mention that Beasts have access to unique powers called Kinship which are inspired by and emulate the powers of other splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T18:13:59-08:00","id":1024037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1023542-sell-me-btp-in-one-sentence?p=1023670#post1023670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Playing a legendary monster straight from the stories. Positioning youself as the Big Bad who is supposed to get his ass kicked by the Designated Good Guy Protagonist, then subverting the plot to seize the role of the Main Character for yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds quite cool.<br /> <br /> and how about Beast being suited for solo games? Werewolf for example socks with solo games, while Changeling works reasonably good and 1E Promethazine seemed to be created with solos in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2637-qendi","name":"qendi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T18:36:14-08:00","id":1024044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>qendi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1023542-sell-me-btp-in-one-sentence?p=1024037#post1024037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That sounds quite cool.<br /> <br /> and how about Beast being suited for solo games? Werewolf for example socks with solo games, while Changeling works reasonably good and 1E Promethazine seemed to be created with solos in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> By solo, do you mean between 1 / 2 players, or just within it's respective universe?<br /> <br /> Like Werewolves, Beasts emphasizes familial bonds and cooperation in order to help each other survive. You can play solo if you want to, but it loses those undertones of being a game about family.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, Beasts feed on the essence of terror. They survive by horrifying (possibly even traumatizing) humans, while justifying their actions as teaching humanity wisdom through fear. This can get rather uncomfortable in a solo game if one player is the ST and the other is describing in details how they're torturing somebody's mind every time they need to recharge their powers. Personally, I would suggest getting more people together in order to distract from that edge, if you don't think you'd be comfortable with it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T18:42:32-08:00","id":1024048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>qendi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1023542-sell-me-btp-in-one-sentence?p=1024037#post1024037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That sounds quite cool.<br /> <br /> and how about Beast being suited for solo games? Werewolf for example socks with solo games, while Changeling works reasonably good and 1E Promethazine seemed to be created with solos in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beast can work quite well as a solo game: Beasts tend to be...the odd women out in a party of other supernatural types, and their feeding habits will probably put off all but the most inhumane creatures. They can perform very well with a niche and can summon their Lairs to their location as a means of giving themselves a major powerup.<br /> <br /> They'd be good if you want to run a character like Beckett from VtM who goes around and studies all of the other supernatural types. An &quot;anthropologist&quot;, if you will. Or as a sort of mediator-for-hire in a region of lots of different supernatural organizations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T18:45:45-08:00","id":1024052,"title":"","content":"Ever play Overlord? Dungeon Keeper? That's Beast. You're the not-quite-evil Overlord, with an expansive Lair that recruits supernatural monsters to you. Build the Lair, grow strong, become a Legend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T18:45:54-08:00","id":1024053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>qendi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1023542-sell-me-btp-in-one-sentence?p=1024037#post1024037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That sounds quite cool.<br /> <br /> and how about Beast being suited for solo games? Werewolf for example socks with solo games, while Changeling works reasonably good and 1E Promethazine seemed to be created with solos in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see anything that would get in the way of solo games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T19:25:56-08:00","id":1024064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1023542-sell-me-btp-in-one-sentence?p=1024044#post1024044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> By solo, do you mean between 1 / 2 players, or just within it's respective universe?<br /> <br /> Like Werewolves, Beasts emphasizes familial bonds and cooperation in order to help each other survive. You can play solo if you want to, but it loses those undertones of being a game about family</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean that I'm stuck in China with only my wife as a player, so solo is 1 to 1 game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2637-qendi","name":"qendi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T21:19:27-08:00","id":1024100,"title":"","content":"Ok, selling Beast the Primordial in once sentence. Haven't read any of the posts after the original, here it goes:<br /> <br /> Beast the Primordial is a game about playing as a monster, and confronts both the players and the characters with the question &quot;Why is a monster a monster?&quot;<br /> <br /> Ok, looking at the other posts now...yes! Didn't copy anyone else directly. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> To elaborate more on my selling sentence, and help with the solo Chronicle question, Beast is a game about being a human who's soul is devoured/fused to a Horror of the Primordial Dream, the layer that separates the Temenos from the Anima Mundi (for those unfamiliar with Astral Realm jargon, from Humanity's shared dream from the World's shared dream.) They become one with the Horror and gain it's otherworldly powers and might, but at the cost of being it's appetite's conduits in the waking world. The more appeased the Horror's Satiety is, the more of yourself you are. The hungrier the Horror's Satiety is the more of an influence it becomes over your normal thoughts and mannerisms. Worse of all though, the Horror is still a part of Humanity's shared dream and therefore influenced by Humanity's subconscious. Enter the Monomyth, a cosmic narrative that dooms the Horror (and the poor sod who's housing it) to meet it's end in some terrible or tragic fashion. No matter what a Begotten tries they will never be able to escape the fate that the Story has written for them. They must feed on fear, they will attract the attention of those who are bound just like them except their role is their slayer, and they will die either at the hands of these &quot;Heroes&quot; or from some other force from the Chronicles of Darkness. A Beast Chronicle is about a Begotten juggling their dual natures as being a part of the world along with humans, monsters, and other stranger things while still being bound to consume human fear no matter their own desires. It's about being a creature of myth and legend yet profoundly dependent upon the humans you must prey upon. It's about trying to break free of the role the story decided you must play, despite the fact that in order to do that you must abandon your humanity entirely and become almost a force of nature all your own. <br /> <br /> Hope that helps. And good luck. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T09:42:39-08:00","id":1024791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1023542-sell-me-btp-in-one-sentence?p=1024052#post1024052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ever play Overlord? Dungeon Keeper? That's Beast. You're the not-quite-evil Overlord, with an expansive Lair that recruits supernatural monsters to you. Build the Lair, grow strong, become a Legend.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is overselling the boss monster potential of the game which still lacks Lair abilities or merits that might simulate the horde of goblins/minions you command in Overlord. Hoping the upcoming supplements fix this oversight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T11:37:09-08:00","id":1024856,"title":"","content":"Beast is Monsters Inc. as made by Guillermo del Toro.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T16:55:01-08:00","id":1024941,"title":"","content":"Batman and the Joker are equally viable character concepts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T02:20:00-08:00","id":1025036,"title":"","content":"<i>&quot;What is better - to be born good, or to overcome your evil nature through great effort?&quot;</i> \u2015Paarthurnax<br /> <br /> That's a Line that was Put about by afew of us while discussing Beast Prior... (Development changed one thing that it relied on but didn't right it off completely, How you become a Beast/Begotten) And it sums up afair bit of the flavour that drew me to supporting it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T03:25:43-08:00","id":1029530,"title":"","content":"&quot;Being a hero, like a beast, is what you make of it.&quot; -Sidebar page 202, B:tP core.<br /> <br /> Now. To elaborate further. Beast: The Primordial is a game where the easy route both as a character and as a player is to be an unapologetic asshole on an IC basis. It strips away all pretenses of morality, of sanity, and the idea that you have to behave in a certain way. Other characters do not have this freedom of amorality. When given this, you have to ask yourself, &quot;I am in a sandbox. Few if any consequences will come my way no matter what I do. What SHOULD I do, even if I can do virtually anything?&quot;. Most won't. Most will look at the freedom and take it at face value. Why not indulge in your power, there's nothing to prevent you. It's what others justify to themselves by believing they have a positive impact, despite abusing random unfortunates who catch their attention. And yet the truth of this all, is the axis upon which the game rests is the most important one. The players. The players do not need to be assholes despite in-character influence, as ultimately they control their character. They have freedom, and what they do with that freedom in a world of monsters is a big thing. They have power, and an environment which encourages petty status wars and competition for its own sake. They're monsters, and they have to hurt other people to survive. Sound familiar? In its own way, Beast: The Primordial is a full-circle reinvention of the classic byline from Vampire: The Masquerade, &quot;A beast I am, lest a beast I become&quot;. And that is of course, compelling in its new form to me. The only challenge is, that the player here is the humanity meter rather than any numbers and a lot of us don't bat an eyelash at playing an unapologetic monster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2532-blitzkitty","name":"BlitzKitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T05:24:37-08:00","id":1029560,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">Well, after reading through more of the book, I'd have to say that Beast is a game about doing the wrong thing for the right reasons. <b>Wisdom through Fear</b>, that's what Beasts contribute to society. While there are Beasts who don't care about humanity and just exist to satiate their appetites, such Beasts are not very welcomed by the rest of their kind. The book explicitly says &quot;eat to live, don't live to eat.&quot;<br /> <br /> As a Beast, you take on the role of the Big Bad Wolf. In the narrative of Grimm's fairy tales, you are the moral of the story. Your job is to teach mankind not to be a bunch of idiots, or else there will be consequences for their actions. Heroes, the game's primary villains, have misinterpreted your actions to be detrimental to society (as opposed to beneficial), and they have dedicated their lives to hunting down and exterminating you whenever possible.<br /> <br /> Of course, none of this changes the fact that as a Beast, you draw nourishment from fear. You need to torment people in order to maintain your self control. If you refuse to do so, very bad shit happens, and that shit attracts more Heroes than it would have if you just maintained a steady diet. Heroes don't understand that your feeding habits are keeping the majority of humanity safe. They only see you as another trophy to be mounted on their wall, and so begins their quest.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T04:23:22-08:00","id":1029997,"title":"","content":"In Beast, you explore the horror behind the world, in every way that phrase can be interpreted.<br /> <br /> To expound... First, you literally do have a horrific monster (and a horrific landscape) behind your worldly body. Second, most of the ways you feed that monster are through ordinary-seeming actions that are part of the normal human world - thus, you can explore the currents of evil and abuse that run through and behind the normal world, and that we accept as part of it. Third, Beasts have a mythology that unifies the supernatural into one family, and a good claim to connection with <i>the</i> horror who birthed them all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}